{"id":"u-3aa6615a-af5f-43b9-8aae-70ebd16ba2ea","src":"community","title":"12-Week High-Yield Workout 🔥❤️‍🔥🐦‍🔥","author":"Jah J.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/OVs6EY-untitled-program","desc":"Split Type: 4-Day Upper/Lower Split\nTarget Frequency: Each muscle group trained 2x per week\nSession Volume: 16–19 total working sets per session\nWeekly Schedule: Train Mon/Tue & Thu/Fri; Rest Wed & Sat/Sun\n\n1. Progressive Overload Tracking: Every single workout, write down your weights and reps. If you hit 4 sets of 8 reps on Bench Press today, your goal next week is 4 sets of 8 reps with 5 extra pounds or hitting 9 reps with the same weight.\n\n2. Rest Durations Matter: Compound lifts (Squat, Bench, Deadlift, OHP) require 2.5 to 3 minutes between heavy sets to replenish ATP stores so you can move maximum load.\n\n3. Recovery Fueling: Match your training intensity with high protein intake (~1.0g per lb of bodyweight daily) and 7–8 hours of quality sleep for tissue repair.\n\nPyramid Feeder Sets: \nAfter the dynamic warm-up, do 2 feeder sets on your main exercise before your working sets:\n\nFeeder 1: 50% working weight × 5 reps (smooth, fast)\n\nFeeder 2: 75% working weight × 2 reps (priming neurological firing, zero fatigue)\n\nPyramid Feeder Sets:\n\nFeeder 1: Empty bar × 8 reps (focus on depth and tempo)\n\nFeeder 2: 60% working weight × 4 reps\n\nFeeder 3: 80% working weight × 1 rep (gets your nervous system ready for the load)\n\n12-Week Periodization Strategy: Clear rep and RIR (Reps in Reserve) targets broken down into Phase 1 (Hypertrophy Base), Phase 2 (Heavy Strength), and Phase 3 (Peak Power).","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-28T08:49:38.598Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["MONDAY- Workout 1- Upper A- Chest and Lats🦍","TUESDAY- Workout lower A- Quad and Core 🚀","Thursday -Workout -Upper B- shoulders, upper back","Friday workout lower B posteri